WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.740
Poverty &amp; Argentina hit 32.3% ending two years of decline for millions. This is Omni View Central &amp; South America, Episode 3. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. Merco Press says the National Institute of Statistics &amp; Censes put that figure out on Thursday for the first half of this year. It sits 4.1 points above the second half of 2025. Yesterday the government said this rise would be published today.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:37.580
The slide since mid-2024 has stopped. Extreme poverty moved from 6.3% to 7.5%, a gain

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:44.800
of 1.2 points. Inside the 31 urban areas of the permanent household survey, 9.7 million

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:51.440
people fell under the poverty line and 2.2 million under the extreme line. Argentine media projecting

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:58.060
those urban readings onto the whole country put poverty at 15.4 to 15.5 million people,

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.920
in extreme poverty near 3.6 million.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:05.420
By household, 24.4% were under the poverty line

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.360
and 5.6% under the extreme line.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.980
Set against the first half of 2025, the moves are smaller.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.060
Poverty was 31.6% then, extreme poverty 6.9%,

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.120
so the gaps are 0.7 and 0.6 points.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:26.620
The second half of 2025 at 28.2%

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:32.800
had been the lowest mark since 2018, when the year ended at 27.3%.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.200
Argentine accounts poverty by income against the cost of a basic basket,

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.000
so inflation moves the line.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.840
In June, a family of four needed 1.5 million pesos to stay above it,

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:49.220
and 689,853 pesos to stay out of extreme poverty.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.040
Children carry more of it.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:55.300
44.5% of those under 14 live in poor households,

00:01:55.300 --> 00:02:03.860
against 36.9% of people 15 to 29 and 28.8% of people 30 to 64. Concordia is

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:11.020
highest among the places named at 56.2%, then Grand Resistencia at 48.6 and

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:18.960
Posadas at 42.2. Around Buenos Aires the outer districts reach 36.9%. The city of

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:26.160
Aris stood at 11.1 percent. Places under 500,000 people rose 4.9 points. Larger

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:31.660
centers rose 3.9. Across the region, Hurricane Polo is bearing down on Baja

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:37.420
California with sustained winds near 150 miles an hour, the Guardian reports, and

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:42.040
gusts stronger than that in the core. On the 22nd of September, the pressure was

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:47.600
892 millibars. That reading makes it the second most intense hurricane on record in

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:52.980
the east Pacific, exceptionally warm Pacific water is feeding it, in a season the paper calls

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:58.460
notably active. The track is expected to bend west, northwest, then more to the northwest

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:04.420
on Saturday. Some wobble and strength is possible. It is still expected to stay powerful as it runs

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:10.540
northwest. Hurricane Force Wind reaches about 40 miles from the center. Tropical Storm Force Wind

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:17.520
reaches about 125. Torrential rain and dangerous seas could hit hard along with that wind. In Nicaragua

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:23.260
A United Nations group of human rights experts has published a 47-page dossier, dated

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:27.720
the 21st of September, under the title, The Anatomy of State Cruelty.

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:30.220
Latin America reports has the account.

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:35.700
The group denounces eight years of government repression, including disappearances and killings.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:43.060
It details 161 in force disappearances since April 2018, when protests over social security

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:48.000
changes became a national challenge to Daniel Ortega, and a violent crackdown left more

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.300
than 300 people dead.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.940
The experts say the methods have widened the range of people targeted, and they point

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:58.820
to what they call coordinated action by several state bodies on a chain of command that reaches

00:03:58.820 --> 00:03:59.700
senior government.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.700
Eight people held on political grounds died with the report calls preventable deaths in

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:05.140
custody.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:10.360
One of them is Brooklyn Rivera-Brayan, a mosquito-indigenous leader, 73.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:24.240
Authorities announced his death on the 31st of May, Ortega and co-president Rosario Mario recently suspended elections indefinitely, a move described in the account as criticized for locking in an effective dictatorship.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:35.940
The dossier splits the repression into four phases, from Operation Cleanup in 2018 to measures after 2023 aimed at absolute control of the state and the population.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:41.760
Also, today, Ecuador has detained dozens of people over suspected links to a Mexican cartel.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:48.100
Latest news from Azerbaijan reports. Shakira put nearly $4 million toward a school in Cartagena,

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:53.960
Colombia, with places for 1,700 students at a school that has worked with the local community

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.420
for more than a decade. La Nassioan reports.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:05:02.640
At the South American Games, the International Pedal Federation says Argentina is in two finals,

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:06.200
goals, with gold medal matches still ahead against Paraguay and Chile.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:11.720
The case on both sides today is whether Argentina should let the peso fall further, and the

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:13.320
two voices are not the government.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:19.760
Guida Gopinath, once number two at the International Monetary Fund, wants a larger drop, plus a

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:22.740
bigger pile of reserves, so activity has a better setting.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:29.120
She told Tyler Cowan of George Mason University in his series Conversations with Tyler, that

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:33.160
But the peso has to adjust more, and should be allowed to depreciate more than it is

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:33.660
doing now.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.880
La Nación carried that on Friday.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:37.640
His reason is the election.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.720
Wait, he says, until that uncertainty clears.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:45.000
Nobody will reasonably add to a local book, and some may trim exposure.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.760
He does not say a weaker peso would be a mistake.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:51.200
He says new money will not come while the vote is unresolved.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:56.020
Both take investor caution as the fact on the ground, and both leave the next step on

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:56.860
an open calendar.

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:02.020
A sign of progress is in Ecuador, where mining weekly says Dynacore's plant rehabilitation

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:06.720
is 65% complete, while the company pushes expansion work forward.

